    {
      "id": "p0256-b013",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "This line is a pun on the phrase \"without reservations\", which normally means \"without any worries\" but also means \"without making advance arrangements\" in this case. Because this English pun would be lost in a literal translation, the localization team replaced it with a Japanese pun on the words yōyaku (\"finally\") and yoyaku (\"reservations; advance arrangements\"):",
        "raw": "This line is a pun on the phrase \"without reservations\", which normally means\n\"without any worries\" but also means \"without making advance arrangements\"\nin this case. Because this English pun would be lost in a literal translation,\nthe localization team replaced it with a Japanese pun on the words yoyaku\n(\"finally\") and yoyaku (\"reservations; advance arrangements\"):",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29136533,
          0.71798571,
          0.89645262,
          0.8036
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28934027,
          0.71727143,
          0.90435035,
          0.80467143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          63,
          64,
          65,
          66,
          67
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "without reservations 通常表示“毫无顾虑”，在这里又指“不必提前预订”。这个英语双关无法直译，团队便换成日语 yōyaku（终于）与 yoyaku（预订）的近音双关：",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 71,
            "italic": true,
            "lang": "en"
          },
          {
